<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The table shows the cumulative frequencies of the masses, in kg (to the nearest kg), of <m>{54}</m> sacks of potatoes at Nyahururu market.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass (kg)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{49}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60}</m>–<m>{69}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{33}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{42}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{51}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{54}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) How many sacks weigh less than <m>{39.5}</m> kg?</p><div><fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) How many sacks weigh <m>{39.5}</m> kg or more?</p><div><fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) How many sacks are in the class <m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m>?</p><div><fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The cumulative frequency at an upper class boundary counts every value below that boundary. So the cumulative frequency of a class counts every sack in that class and in all the classes before it.</p><p>(a) <m>{39.5}</m> kg is the upper class boundary of <m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m>, so <m>{33}</m> sacks weigh less than it.</p><p>(b) <m>{33}</m> sacks weigh less than <m>{39.5}</m> kg, so <m>{54} - {33} = {21}</m> weigh <m>{39.5}</m> kg or more.</p><p>(c) Subtract the cumulative frequency of the class before: <m>{51} - {42} = {9}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>33</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>21</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>9</m></p></answer>
